# <%= module %>

```console
mix deps.get
mix test
mix nerves_gate.sim --firmware path/to/nerves_gate.fw
mix nerves_gate.sim.install
mix nerves_gate.package
```

`mix test` runs ordinary host unit tests. Device services come only from a real
gateway: there is no fake SDK backend. `mix nerves_gate.sim` starts disposable
QEMU gateways running real Nerves Gate firmware (Linux, QEMU, `fwup` and
`mkfs.ext4` required). Start the devices on the simulator site, then run
`mix nerves_gate.sim.install` in another terminal to package this application
and run it through the device's application manager and virtual SD card. Use the
site's manual controls to unplug cables or disturb the uplink.

Packaging builds production code (without the simulator) into
`<%= app %>-1.0.0.ez`. Install it through the device's administrative
`NervesGate.Apps.install/1` API, then `NervesGate.Apps.start(:<%= app %>)`.
Application code and `NervesGateSDK.Storage.data_dir(:<%= app %>)` live on SD;
platform configuration does not. Handle unavailable storage explicitly.

Packages run trusted code in the firmware BEAM, not a sandbox. Do not bundle
platform libraries or use internal firmware modules. Private dependencies are
bundled; native code must be built for the device architecture. Upgrades are
cold restarts with a bounded `health_check/0`, not OTP hot-code upgrades.
